Package: dataexcept
Title: Structured, Classed Failures that Cross Language Boundaries
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Diogo", "Ribeiro", email = "dfr@esmad.ipp.pt",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-2022-7072"))
Description: Classed error conditions for data and modelling workflows that
    carry structured fields and machine-readable recovery metadata (whether a
    failure is transient or permanent, and whether a retry can succeed), and
    that serialise to the language-neutral failure envelope published by the
    'DataExcept' 'Python' package, so failures written by 'R' and 'Python'
    code share one format. Envelopes from either language can be read back
    into 'R' conditions. Credentials in URLs are redacted before they reach a
    condition or an envelope. A companion layer gives classes to the warnings
    base 'R' and 'stats' signal with only a message, recognising them through
    the translated message catalogue so the match holds in any session
    language.
